### Round 2 report
Resumed E8-T08 for the three points of the round-1 verification (E92) only. Points 1 and 3 change code; point 2 changes evidence only. Each change has a test seen failing first (`20`, `19`, `28`). No API contract, catalog, parameter, event, notification, error code or audit action changed.

**Point 1: mandate counter (review #1).** Every writer that replaces `member.paymentMethod` now goes through `CensusRules.keepMandateSequence(slug, memberNumber, previous, replacement)`. It keeps the highest of the old and new sequences. It only counts this member's own `{{slug}}-{{number}}-{{n}}` references, and it only copies a saved counter when there is no member number.
- `SignupService.card` (signup / add-dog Checkout completion, the review's line 161) keeps the counter.
- `applyReadmission` carries the LEFT record's counter onto the submitted method, whatever its type.
- Validation's mandate (old line 1010) now uses the four-argument `mandateRef` with `lastMandateSequence` of the record. A SEPA readmission after MANUAL/CARD therefore signs `-2`, not `-1`.
- `BillingCensusAdapter.saveCard` and the pending-signup edit in `MemberService` use the same helper. The second could only carry a saved counter.
- The counter is still never serialized: two tests assert `GET /members/{id}` has no `lastMandateSequence`.

**Point 2: whitespace evidence (review #2).** `27-diff-check-published-before.log` reproduces the reviewer's `git diff --check a218eea^ a218eea` → **exit 2**, 169 findings, all in this task's evidence logs. `normalize-whitespace.py` strips only line-end and end-of-file whitespace from every `roadmap/evidence/E8-T08/*.log`, including round 1's logs (`36`). The content is otherwise unchanged. `diff-check.py` runs `git diff --check HEAD` over tracked changes and `git diff --no-index --check /dev/null <file>` over every untracked file. It is read-only: no index or ref is written. As a negative control before normalizing (`28`), it exits **2** with 182 findings in the new logs, while plain `git diff --check HEAD` exits 0 — the reviewer's point.

**Point 3: CI's dependency audit (red since `7b5521d`).** I reproduced it locally on the packaged jar with the pinned Trivy 0.74.0: `19-audit-before.log`, exit 1, `fixableCritical: CVE-2026-47884 org.springframework:spring-webmvc` (installed 6.2.19, fixed 7.0.9). Upgrading on this line is not possible:
- `./mvnw -U dependency:get -Dartifact=org.springframework:spring-webmvc:6.2.20` → `Could not find artifact … in central`;
- `spring-boot-dependencies:3.5.17` is absent too;
- the only fix is Spring Framework 7 (Spring Boot 4), a migration well beyond this task.

So the change is a justified, time-limited suppression, and the policy now has a written mechanism for it:
- `bin/security-scan` reads `bin/security-scan-suppressions.json`. An entry applies only to its exact `id` + `package` + `installedVersion`. It must carry `reason`, `task`, `recorded` and `expires`, with the expiry at most 90 days after `recorded`; otherwise the audit fails with `ValueError`.
- An expired entry stops applying, so the finding blocks again.
- Suppressed findings are printed under `suppressedCritical` with their fixed version, expiry and advisory title; expired ids go under `expiredSuppressions`.
- The advisory title Trivy reports is «Remote Code Execution via improper path limitation in XsltView». The api renders no server-side views: no `XsltView`, `ViewResolver`, `ModelAndView` or plain `@Controller` exists in `src/main`. The new `ArchitectureTest.E8_T08_noXsltServerSideViews` keeps it that way.
- The entry expires on **2026-12-07** (60 days).
- `bin/security-scan-test.py` gains four policy tests: exact match only, expiry, malformed or over-long entries, and the committed file is valid.
- `docs/DEPLOY.md`'s scan paragraph documents the mechanism.
- The other 16 findings are HIGH/MEDIUM: report-only under the existing policy and unchanged (see proposals).

