### Round 2 assumptions
1. A card completion during a pending readmission still writes into the submitted method (E38). That is safe because `applyReadmission` now carries the counter. Migration re-apply (`PlayoffPlanner`/`MigrationApplyService`) is a pre-cutover import that already keeps an existing `mandateRef`, so I left it unchanged.
2. «The scan policy allows» had no written mechanism. I added one in `bin/security-scan` with a 90-day maximum and a 60-day first expiry (2026-12-07). The image scan (`security-image` job) applies the same file. I could not run that job's image scan locally (it needs a Docker image build); it was skipped in the failing run because it depends on `dependency-audit`. The whole CI run on the published commit is the organizer's handoff.
3. Normalizing round 1's logs changes whitespace only. Their exits and content are what the round-1 report quotes.

### Round 2 questions / catalog proposals
- **Denied command:** `xmllint --noout --schema src/main/resources/sepa/pain.008.001.02.xsd src/test/resources/sepa/remesa-2026-09.golden.xml` (and the same for `target/sepa/remesa-2026-09.actual.xml`) was denied in this session. The equivalent evidence is above. Direct Trivy invocations (`.local/security-tools/trivy-0.74.0 rootfs …`) were denied too; `bin/security-scan` was allowed and is CI's actual command.
- **Proposal (nonblocking, before 2026-12-07):** a task to move to Spring Boot 4 / Spring Framework 7, or to adopt a fixed 6.2.x if Spring publishes one. It would remove the suppression.
- **Proposal:** I chose not to touch the report-only HIGH findings, to keep this task's scope (`jackson-core`/`jackson-databind` 2.21.4 → same-line 2.21.7, `httpcore5` 5.3.6). They could join that dependency task.
- No catalog change.
